From: Suderra OS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] env: flag the RAUC boot counters as the writeable variables

U-Boot 2025.04 has no Kconfig symbol for the static environment flag list
that CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST needs; boards set CFG_ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC in
their config header (include/configs/hmibsc.h does the same for these three
variables). The list lives in the one header every board includes through
env_flags.h so the production Raspberry Pi U-Boot and the QEMU U-Boot that
tests its boot chain share it (ADR-048 DEC-18, EI-034).

Applies to U-Boot v2025.04 (sha256 of the tarball in buildroot/boot/uboot).
---
 include/env_flags.h | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/include/env_flags.h
+++ b/include/env_flags.h
@@ -38,7 +38,13 @@
 #define ENV_FLAGS_VARACCESS_LOC 1
 
 #ifndef CFG_ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC
-#define CFG_ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC ""
+/*
+ * Suderra OS: with CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST the stored environment may change
+ * only the variables flagged "w" here (U-Boot 2025.04 has no Kconfig symbol for
+ * this list). They are the RAUC boot counters; every other variable, bootcmd
+ * and bootargs among them, comes from the compiled-in default environment.
+ */
+#define CFG_ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC "BOOT_ORDER:sw,BOOT_A_LEFT:dw,BOOT_B_LEFT:dw"
 #endif
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_NET
